# Transaction

A transaction start page explains a task and directs users to the service that performs it. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/transaction/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## Task entry has its own owner

The [start-page pattern](../../patterns/start-page.html) owns prerequisites and a clear destination. [Question pages](../../patterns/question-pages.html#compose-the-task-without-replacing-its-owner) own the answers if the supported flow actually asks questions. This publishing template remains a task-entry composition; it cannot establish a backend, save or device action by presentation alone.

## When to use it

Use this structure when a household task needs context before opening the native HA flow or an external service. Explain what the person can do, what they need and where they will go. Common immediate device controls do not need a separate start page.

## Structure and behaviour

Use a task-oriented title and one clear primary destination. A link that opens a flow is navigation; an action that immediately operates a device needs a button and the existing command safeguards. Explain any external account or service boundary before the person leaves.

## Home Assistant boundary

This reference does not create device commands or bypass authentication. Avoid a vague “Start now” label when “Open theme settings” conveys the task. Never link to an unverified local route or make a documentation button appear to operate the household.

